---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { getMeta } from '../lib/data';
import { formatNumber } from '../lib/formatters';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
const m = getMeta();
---

<Prose title="About ZIPCodeDetails – Independent US ZIP Code Reference" description="ZIPCodeDetails is a free, independent reference for every US ZIP code, built on public data from the US Census Bureau and USPS." heading="About ZIPCodeDetails" crumb="About" path="/about/">
  <p class="lead">{SITE.brand} is a free, independent reference for US ZIP codes. We turn public government data into fast, readable pages for {formatNumber(m.zip_count)} ZIP codes, {formatNumber(m.city_count)} cities and towns, and {formatNumber(m.county_count)} counties.</p>

  <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A page for every standard and PO Box ZIP code: city, county, time zone, map, population, income, home values and nearby ZIP codes.</li>
    <li>City, county and state pages listing every ZIP code with sortable data.</li>
    <li>Free tools: <a href="/what-is-my-zip-code/">What’s my ZIP code?</a>, a <a href="/tools/zip-code-distance/">distance calculator</a> and a <a href="/tools/zip-code-radius/">radius search</a>.</li>
    <li><a href="/rankings/">Rankings</a> of the richest, most expensive and most populated ZIP codes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
  <p>Everything is built from public-domain datasets published by the US Census Bureau and the US Postal Service. Our <a href="/data-sources/">data sources &amp; methodology</a> page explains exactly what we use and the known limitations.</p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to the United States Postal Service. For official address validation, always use <a href="https://tools.usps.com/zip-code-lookup.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USPS.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
  <p>The site is free to use and supported by advertising and, on some pages, clearly labeled partner links. Advertisers never influence our data. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>Spotted something wrong? <a href="/contact/">Tell us</a> — we read every message and fix verified errors in the next update.</p>
</Prose>
